# ROADMAP — Project Status, Release Pin & Active Sprint Backlog

File: openOODA/ROADMAP.oot
NORTHSTAR is the vision. SHIPPED is what exists. ROADMAP is the active plan.
Rebuilt from NORTHSTAR vs disk (phalanx 2026-08-16). C emit + gcc remains the product path.

## 1. Pin

  Release: v0.205.0-beta. Product libraries: `ooda/std`. GitHub `openOODA/std` archived. Not a volume cert.
  Product tip (ooda): main. Boards tip: main. Libraries: `ooda/std` on product tip.
  Status: compiler/CLI floor shipped (OPEN-1..92 checked). Libraries live in `ooda/std`. Named emit+gcc+run still required.

## 2. Rebuild

  From `ooda/`:
    export PURE_NO_ARC=0
    OODAC_BIN=./bootstrap/seed/oodac bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build oodac/main.oo oodac/oodac
    OODAC_BIN=./oodac/oodac bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build oodac/main.oo oodac/oodac
    ./oodac/oodac check oodac/main.oo
  Official rebuild is `bootstrap/oodac_pure_build`. `PURE_SKIP_CHECK=1` is opt-in only.
  `oodac check scripts/ci_product.oo` typechecks rails. It does not emit, gcc, or run them.
  Named emit+gcc+run proof is `scripts/ci_open_run.oo`.

## 3. Status words

  done — works, proved on disk
  smoke — small check passes
  partial — part works
  residual — wanted in NORTHSTAR, not yet built
  open — active sprint task
  stale — old leftover words; a later proof closed them

## 4. NORTHSTAR vs disk

  Live check: RAM-cold `oodac check oodac/main.oo` about 164s; disk-warm new-process about 0.02s (179 modules). Not under 10s cold.
  Memory: `PURE_NO_ARC=0`. Memory is freed when the last reference drops.
  Native path: no wasmtime, clang, or special env file for C emit + gcc.
  Std: product tree is `ooda/std`. Floor folders first (power law). Domain folders unproved.
  Agent tools (1.1): JSON diagnostics, outline, reflect, fix, patch — done.
  Runtime (1.2): ARC, spawn, arenas, Landlock, rlimit — done. Pause-free GC and undo-RAM stay later.
  Language (2–4): must-use Result/Option, Option/Result exhaust, E_CAP, const header fold — done.
  Caps / SECRET: missing token and `process_exec` sink refuse — done. Full IFC is a moonshot.
  Backends: C emit + `chs_rt` + gcc is the product path. LLVM hello lock is product. Extra emit-x86 writes open69 Hello, folds hello.oo greet, harvests const ALU/if/let/mix, leftover-plus-print and while/for leftover ERR, SysV rdi/rsi/frame, bump concat, and greet `call` (`scripts/x86_*_smoke.oo`; not a complete backend). Extra emit-wasm writes `\0asm`. Print-lit, hello greet fold, same-fn ident-let, N-string const strcat, two-println, three-println, int-lit println, const INT+INT, if-true/if-false, if-true-no-else, if INT==INT, if INT!=INT, if-false-no-else, four-println, five-println, six-println, seven-println, eight-println, nine-println, ten-println, eleven-println, twelve-println, thirteen-println, fourteen-println, fifteen-println, sixteen-println, seventeen-println, const else-if, INT+INT+INT, INT-INT, INT*INT, INT/INT, INT%INT, unary-minus println, bool true/false println, if INT<INT, if INT>INT, if INT<=INT, if INT>=INT, if !true/!false, if BOOL&&BOOL, if BOOL||BOOL, if (true), if (INT==INT), if (INT!=INT), if (INT<INT), if (INT>INT), if (INT<=INT), if (INT>=INT), if INT==INT no-else, if INT!=INT no-else, if INT<INT no-else, if INT>INT no-else, if INT<=INT no-else, if INT>=INT no-else, if !false no-else, if BOOL&&BOOL no-else, if BOOL||BOOL no-else, if (true) no-else, if (INT==INT) no-else, if (INT!=INT) no-else, if (INT<INT) no-else, if (INT>INT) no-else, if (INT<=INT) no-else, if (INT>=INT) no-else, if (BOOL&&BOOL) no-else, if (BOOL||BOOL) no-else, if (!false) no-else, nested if true no-else, if INT==INT && INT==INT no-else, if INT==INT || INT==INT no-else, if (INT==INT && INT==INT) no-else, if (INT==INT || INT==INT) no-else, if !(INT==INT) no-else, if ((true)) no-else, if INT!=INT && INT!=INT no-else, if (!(INT==INT)) no-else, if INT!=INT || INT!=INT no-else, if (INT!=INT && INT!=INT) no-else, if INT<INT && INT<INT no-else, and nested if true are named locks. Mixed ident concat stays dummy. Hostile second print stays dummy. IDENT if stays dummy. IDENT a