  Compiler — C emit + gcc + `chs_rt` (pin `v0.205.0-beta`; `audit/library_status.oot` 137 GREEN / 4279 BLOCKED):

  Ranked next:
  1. import+call gcc (`recv.m(args)` is not a C member call)
  2. `timeout 30` emit-c of encoding/text floor (354 TIMEOUT)
  3. named `ERR\tc_emit` for walk SEMI / slist OOB (not abort 134)
  4. `Result[List[Name]]` emit (`OoResL_Name`; fail lock today)
  5. contract DOT (`requires s.len() > 0` is `requires residual`)

  C language (emit-c + gcc + chs_rt):

  [ ] import+call gcc: user method is a C call or `->`, not `recv.m(args)`. Imported typedefs and Result cells. Lock: `scripts/import_call_gcc_smoke.oo`. Leftover methods stay `ERR\tc_emit`. (residual: leftover methods)
  [ ] Contract DOT methods: `requires s.len() > 0` lowers (`oo_chars_len`). Lock: `scripts/contract_method_smoke.oo`. Other contract ops stay `requires residual`. (residual: non-`chars_len` ops)
  [ ] `Result[List[Name]]` emit is `OoResL_Name` and gcc+runs. Lock: `scripts/result_ll_name_smoke.oo`. `Result[Option]` and `Result[Int, Bool]` stay `ERR\tc_emit`. (residual: `Result[Option]`, `Result[Int, Bool]`)
  [ ] C `if` / `match` as expressions (not only stmt / `let y = if`). Lock: `scripts/c_if_expr_smoke.oo`. (no residual needed: pure expr form)
  [ ] `for` expr bounds (`0..(n-1)`, `0..list_len(xs)`) and typed `List[Name]` elem. Lock: `scripts/for_expr_bound_smoke.oo`. (residual: typed `List[Name]` elem)

